2. We implemented a fix that uses regular expressions to find tags anywhere in the text, not just after spaces. The new implementation:
   - Uses a regex pattern `#(\w+)` to find all tags
   - Captures the text after the # character
   - Preserves the order of appearance
   - Handles tags in various contexts (after spaces, commas, inside parentheses, etc.)

3. We added comprehensive test cases to verify the function works correctly for all scenarios.

